.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 534 AM PDT Mon Jul 27 2026

The marine is shallow this morning, with MVFR cigs found around
coastal Bay Area locations and IFR cigs around Monterey Bay. These
clouds should begin to erode by mid morning, with clear skies by
late morning for the majority of the region. Breezy onshore winds
are expected to pick up this afternoon and evening with most sites
being around 10 to 20kt with gusts up to 30kt. Winds begin to
decrease after sunset and then the question becomes will the marine
layer try to deepen tonight. Guidance shows it may similar to today,
perhaps between 500-1000ft. Confidence for stratus return is highest
along the coast and near Monterey Bay.

Vicinity of SFO...Stratus is hanging out around the southern portion
of the San Francisco Bay this morning, leading to MVFR ceilings at
KOAK and KSFO. KHAF has just dropped their ceiling into IFR
territory, which may bleed over to KSFO around or shortly after
sunrise. Confidence is low in this occuring, thus no AMD occuring
after this AFD posts, but it will worth monitoring and adjusting if
it does occur. Given the marine layer is shallower this morning,
expect clearing to occur by late morning, with VFR cigs holding
through at least the early evening hours. Guidance beyond then,
shows the possibility of stratus returning tonight, perhaps after 9Z-
10Z. Confidence remains low on the stratus given how tonight has
panned out, thus hinted at the possibility of this rather than
locking it in.

The other forecast concern for SFO will be the increasing onshore
winds this afternoon. Look for winds to be around 15kt this morning
and then increase to roughly 15-20kt this afternoon, with gusts up to
30kt expected. Winds begin to ease around after sunset, with gusts
to 20-25kt possible until 6Z.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Stratus has filled in around the southern
portion of the Bay, slinking down the Salinas Valley, and creeping
into coastal Santa Cruz County. Look IFR cigs to hold through mid to
late morning before clear skies return. Breezy onshore winds pick up
this afternoon, where will gusts to 15 to 20kt at the TAF sites,
locally higher down the Salinas Valley and the Big Sur Coast.
Stratus looks to return later tonight. Confidence is medium on the
stratus return time.

